-- 168 bits, FAILS (ok=0 fail=667, no normal form). The variable arm asks for
-- its own rest by projection, `intL F list`: intL F list = F list1 (intL F
-- list) = intL F list, an unproductive loop. A rest can only be recomputed
-- by the parser, and the parser's rests all originate in a variable arm, so
-- the arm's own skip cannot be a projection.
(\x. x x) (\x. (\intL. \cont. \list.
  list (\a. a) (\u. list (\q. cont) (intL (\k1 \k2. k2) list))
    (\bit1. intL (\exp. bit1
      (cont (\args \arg. exp (\zx \zy. zx arg (zy args))))
      (intL (\exp2. cont (\args. exp args (exp2 args)))))))
  (x x))
